  "description": "Veto exception at the boundary: exactly one survivor is 'fewer than two', so all vetoes are ignored; the resulting pair tie leaves no Condorcet winner and a Copeland tie, decided by approval",
  "spec_clause": "Phase 2 / Veto: 'if vetoes leave fewer than two finalists, ignore them for ranking' + Phase 2 / Tally resolution order 1 (Copeland) and 2 (Approval count)",
  "rationale": "4 attendees, three finalists (m1 yes 4 / approval 1.00, m2 yes 3 / 0.75, m3 yes 2 / 0.50, all coverage 1.00). u4 vetoes m1 and u3 vetoes m2, both reaching VETO_THRESHOLD 1, which would leave only m3: 1 < 2 -> exception fires, vetoes ignored for ranking, all three go to the round robin. Pairs: m1 vs m2 = 2 (u1,u2) to 2 (u3,u4) -> tie, no winner for that pair; m1 vs m3 = 4-0 m1; m2 vs m3 = 3 (u1,u2,u3) to 1 (u4) -> m2. Copeland: m1 = 1 (beat m3 only), m2 = 1 (beat m3 only), m3 = 0. No finalist beats every other, so there is no Condorcet winner. Rung 1 Copeland: tie between m1 and m2 at 1. Rung 2 approval: m1 1.00 > m2 0.75 -> winner m1. Side effects: u4's yes on m1 -> no, u3's yes on m2 -> no.",
